.\" polinrider(1). Every flag in ACCEPTED in src/cli.rs must appear here;
.\" a test in src/cli.rs fails when one does not. The website's
.\" docs-site/src/content/docs/reference/options.md says the same at length.
.TH POLINRIDER 1 "" "polinrider" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
polinrider \- find and clean up after the PolinRider supply-chain campaign
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B polinrider
.br
.B polinrider check
.RI [ options ]
.IR ROOT ...
.br
.B polinrider clean
.RI [ options ]
.IR REPO ...
.br
.B polinrider guide
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B polinrider \-\-purge\-evidence
.RB [ \-\-evidence
.IR DIR ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B polinrider
checks a computer, a folder or a disk for the PolinRider campaign: the
payload appended to build configs, editor tasks that run on folder open, fake
fonts, known-bad packages and hijacked releases, what starts by itself, and
the
.B MicrosoftSystem64
implant. It also reads the git history of each repository it finds.
.PP
It reports unless told to act. Nothing is ever deleted: with
.B \-\-apply
confirmed files are moved into a quarantine folder that says how to put them
back.
.PP
An option a command cannot use is refused, never ignored. The run stops with
exit status 3 and nothing is scanned.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B polinrider
The guided flow. Asks what to check, one question at a time, and changes
something only when you type
.BR yes .
.TP
.B guide
The same guided flow, spelled out so it can take options.
.TP
.BI check " ROOT..."
Scan the folders given and this computer, and report. A line with folders and
no command is a
.BR check .
.TP
.BI clean " REPO..."
Scan the folders given. With
.BR \-\-apply ,
also cut a payload appended to a build config out of the file in place,
keeping the infected original in quarantine. Never changes git.
.TP
.B \-\-purge\-evidence
Delete the copies of GitHub repositories the guided flow kept, after a typed
.BR yes .
Nothing else is deleted.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS What to scan
.TP
.B \-\-fs\-only
Only the folders given. Reads nothing of this computer: no processes, live
connections, crontab, startup items, editor or app startup files, and no home
folder unless one is named with
.BR \-\-home .
Git history inside the folders is still read.
.B check
only. Cannot be used with
.BR \-\-host\-state .
.TP
.BI \-\-home " DIR"
The home folder to check. Default: the home folder of the user running
.BR polinrider ,
or none under
.BR \-\-fs\-only .
Reports and quarantine folders go here by default too.
.B check
and the guided flow.
.TP
.BI \-\-host\-state " DIR"
Read processes, sockets and crontab from files in
.IR DIR ,
not from this computer.
.B check
and the guided flow. Cannot be used with
.BR \-\-fs\-only .
.SS Git history
By default each repository found is read: the last commit, the staged files,
every branch, remote branch and tag, and every stash, with at most two minutes
per repository. Git is read, never changed.
.TP
.B \-\-git\-all
Also read every earlier commit and every object git keeps. Slower, with no
time limit.
.B check
only. Cannot be used with
.BR \-\-no\-git .
.TP
.B \-\-no\-git
Read no git history. The files on disk, git hooks included, are checked as
before. For a fresh checkout of one commit, as in CI. Never use it on a
computer being cleaned: git can still hold the payload.
.B check
and
.BR clean .
Cannot be used with
.BR \-\-git\-all .
.SS Changing things
.TP
.B \-\-apply
Act on what is confirmed. With
.BR check ,
move each confirmed file into quarantine; it never edits a file. With
.BR clean ,
also cut an appended payload out of a build config. Never deletes a file and
never changes git, a crontab, a shell startup file, a profile, a Run entry or
a scheduled task.
.B check
and
.BR clean .
Cannot be used with
.BR \-\-resume .
.TP
.BI \-\-quarantine " DIR"
Where moved files go, with a
.B manifest.tsv
and a
.BR RESTORE.txt .
Default: a new
.BI polinrider\-quarantine\- DATE
folder in the home folder. Keep it outside the folders being scanned and
outside any git checkout.
.SS The report
.TP
.BI \-\-report " FILE"
Write the full report here. Default:
.BI polinrider\-report\- DATE .txt
in the home folder. Written as the scan goes, so a stopped scan keeps what it
found.
.SS Long scans
A
.B check
saves its place every 5,000 files of step 2. Run the same command again and
it asks whether to continue.
.TP
.B \-\-resume
Continue a stopped check without asking. Only when the version, indicators,
folders and options are the same.
.B check
only. Cannot be used with
.B \-\-fresh
or
.BR \-\-apply .
.TP
.B \-\-fresh
Start again without asking.
.B check
only. Cannot be used with
.BR \-\-resume .
Accepted with
.BR \-\-apply ,
which always starts again.
.SS Indicators
.TP
.BI \-\-ioc " DIR"
The indicator set. Default: the
.B ioc
folder beside the binary, or
.B share/polinrider/ioc
above it. Needs
.IR DIR /strong.txt.
A set that is missing or cannot be read stops the run with exit status 3
before any file is read.
.SS The guided flow and GitHub
.TP
.BI \-\-evidence " DIR"
Where the guided flow keeps copies of GitHub repositories. Default:
.B polinrider\-evidence
in the system's temporary folder. Refused inside a git checkout.
.TP
.BI \-\-forge\-state " DIR"
Read GitHub's answers from files in
.IR DIR ,
not from GitHub. Guided flow only.
.SS Information
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
The version, the commit it was built from and the indicator counts.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
The short list of commands and options.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Clean against the current indicator set. Not proof: signatures rotate.
.TP
.B 1
Review items only. Nothing confirmed.
.TP
.B 2
A confirmed indicator.
.TP
.B 3
The scan could not run, including every refused option. Says nothing about
whether you are infected.
.SH EXAMPLES
Check this computer and a folder, changing nothing:
.PP
.RS
.B polinrider check ~/code
.RE
.PP
Check a backup drive and nothing of this computer:
.PP
.RS
.B polinrider check \-\-fs\-only /Volumes/Backup
.RE
.PP
Clean the repositories in a folder, keeping every original in quarantine:
.PP
.RS
.B polinrider clean \-\-apply ~/code
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git (1)
.PP
Every option at length: https://polinriderscanner.com/docs/reference/options/
.PP
Source and releases: https://github.com/meSingh/polinrider-scanner
